WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.930
A factory in the United States
sells a machine for 50,000 dollars.

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.660
A buyer in Europe pays in euros.

3
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.920
Last year, that meant 50,000 euros.

4
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.460
This year the factory hasn't
changed its price at all.

5
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.980
But the dollar has moved,

6
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.140
and so has the buyer's bill.

7
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.000
So when a country's
money loses value abroad,

8
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.750
who wins and who loses at home?

9
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.130
In this mission, you'll convert
prices across the border,

10
00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.510
from dollars to euros and back.

11
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.390
Then you'll push the exchange
rate in the graph lab,

12
00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:35.790
and watch real GDP and
the price level respond.

13
00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:39.020
Your mission: find out
who gains and who pays

14
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.440
when a currency falls.
